As a Construction Manager - Utility-Scale BESS Consultant, your responsibilities will be the following: 
 Construction and Site Management 
 Lead daily site construction activities from mobilization through commissioning, energization, and project handover;
 Manage EPC contractors, subcontractors, suppliers, and multidisciplinary project teams;
 Conduct site coordination meetings, monitor progress, and resolve field issues through RFIs and approved changes;
 Coordinate logistics, construction sequencing, site access, and operational readiness.
 BESS Technical and Commissioning Oversight 
 Oversee installation of BESS equipment including battery systems, PCS, transformers, switchgear, communications, SCADA, HVAC, and fire protection systems;
 Coordinate SAT, pre-commissioning, functional testing, integrated testing, utility witness testing, and energization activities;
 Manage RFIs, technical queries, design clarifications, deficiencies, NCRs, and commissioning documentation;
 Track testing results, punch lists, corrective actions, and commissioning readiness;
 Provide daily construction updates, issue logs, and risk escalation to project leadership.
 Procurement, Contracts and Trade Management 
 Support procurement activities, bid evaluations, contract administration, and subcontractor management;
 Track long-lead equipment deliveries, vendor support, material shortages, and site inventories;
 Manage subcontractor performance, variations, claims, and contractual correspondence.
 Schedule, Cost and Reporting 
 Maintain project schedules using Primavera P6 or MS Project, including critical path and recovery planning;
 Monitor project progress, manpower, productivity, costs, risks, and change orders;
 Prepare daily and weekly reports, dashboards, meeting minutes, and management updates.
 HSE, Quality and Regulatory Compliance 
 Lead site HSE coordination and ensure compliance with Ontario OHSA requirements;
 Implement quality plans, inspections, test documentation, deficiency management, and turnover packages;
 Coordinate regulatory inspections, permits, and compliance with applicable industry standards and project specifications.
 Stakeholder Coordination 
 Act as the primary on-site contact for clients, utilities, contractors, OEMs, and regulatory authorities;
 Coordinate with engineering and project teams on constructability, technical issues, commissioning readiness, and project delivery.
